Scion: what the KDK archive supplies and the open release leaves out.

Modifications to Apple's xnu (xnu-12377.121.6) and new files for it, Apple Public
Source License 2.0 (APSL-2.0); see https://www.opensource.apple.com/apsl/. Original
files: Apple Inc. These changes: Scion contributors. Apply in order after buildfix.sh.

New osfmk/arm64/scion_vmapple_glue.c and scion_chkstk.s, in place of amcc_rorgn_*.c
(not in the release): no read-only region (the answers of a board without kernel
integrity hardware; text stays writable to the kernel, as on Scion's xnu-8796 builds),
ml_enable_monitor (nothing to enable), ml_device_is_prod_fused (TRUE), the DEVELOPMENT
pmap_pending_preemption, CleanPoC_DcacheRegion_Force_nopreempt[_nohid], and a
__chkstk_darwin with a BTI landing pad (Xcode's libcc_kext copy has none, and the kernel
calls it through an authenticated pointer with BTI enforced).

